npn 7p-7a (see also carevue flownotes for objective data)

dx: sepsis; UTI; pna

Pt's initial lactate 6.9 (12:30 p.m. ER yesterday), after approx 5 1/2 litres NS, including 3 500 cc NS IV boluses, lactate 1.5 this a.m. at 04:15; pt afebrile overnight; received 1st dose Vanco at 19:00, pt needs trough drawn before next dose;

Mildly sedated to be able to be comfortable with vent, fent at 15 mcg/hr, and midaz at 3 mg/ hr; Pt appears comfortable most of the time, does comes bothered with noxious stimuli (suctioning); pulled at OGT last eve approx 21:00, so wrist restraints in use to avoid self-extubation; pt's fingers stiff/contracted, appears chronic condition;
   pt non-communicative w/ nurse, pt w/ hx baseline dimentia; also now w/ sepsis and sedation;

NPO except meds at this time; OGT to low wall sxn, draining clear green bilious return unless pt has recently received opaque med;
   no coffee ground return, no melana or tarry stool; had small amount thin liquid brown stool once when turned and was coughing; specimen sent as ordered;

SCD's in use; pt w/ hct drop from 40 to 28.8 of this a.m.; pt likely dehydrated at time of 40 value, (creatinine 1.7 at that time and is now 0.7 after approx 6 l NS IV hydration); no bruising noted on back when turned;
   Pt's hrt rate at beginning of shift was low 100's, NST w/ occasional to rare PVC's; throughout the night, after IVF's and sedation, pt's hrt rate 80's at rest;

Pt's a.m. serum K+ adequate, phos low--pt w/ new order for pot. phos. 15 mmol, not avail from pharmacy as of 06:30;

PLAN:
1) possible abd CT today
2) pt may need increase in sedation, may also then need vasopressors, discussed with MF
3) vanco trough to be drawn approx 06:30
4) transfuse 2 units PRBC's as soon as available
